ng scale this was the world  record size pavement art 440 feet long  one of the interesting geometrical parts  of this work is that the bottom part of  the work was done on the ground at full  size so while the bottom of the painting  where the people are standing was  painted on the pavement itself on this  it's actually an airstrip the part above  where this panoramic part was painted on  a curved panel much smaller which was  suspended from scaffolding so the shot  is a camera shooting through this curved  panel which is cut out here and then  seeing the enormous pavement art  underneath with all the people standing  on it most of whom were the artists that  helped execute this work  Kurt's art has always been a consuming  passion fascinated by how he can plant  the extraordinary in the midst of every  day  how much time have I spent in life  thinking about this I think I've spent  my entire life thinking about this  starting from when I was eight years old  I'm 64 years old so that puts me at well  over half a century that I've been  thinking about these problems is this  similar to how you model your pieces  yeah that's exactly how I model my  pieces especially before when I was  doing them before we had photography and  Photoshop and all of that a drawing is  in scale which means that these grid  lines here each are one inch by one inch  they correspond to one foot by one foot  in real life this little model here is  about five and a half inches tall as is  this one and then this would tell me  that a person standing with an eye level  of five and a half feet standing here in  a person five and a half feet standing  at the back end of an eight foot by ten  foot image this will appear in a certain  way with a lens which is at this  particular distance which we fixed and  this particular height and is centered  on the pavement surface  and the iPhone then is going to tell me  in the viewfinder what a person would  see now the first thing to do though is  to get 